    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "An update is available for dhcpcd.\nThis update affects Rocky Linux 10.\nA Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE list",
        "title": "Topic"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "The dhcpcd package provides a minimalistic network configuration daemon that supports IPv4 and IPv6 configuration including configuration discovery through NDP, DHCPv4 and DHCPv6 protocols.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* dhcpcd: dhcpcd infinite loop and out-of-bounds read via zero-length IPv6 ND option in Router Advertisement handling (CVE-2026-14258)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n\nThis advisory is provided by Ctrl IQ, Inc for Rocky Linux systems. For more information about CIQ security practices, visit https://ciq.com/security.",
        "title": "Description"
      },
      {
